cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AI Recommendation Consistency Dataset: Run-to-Run Consistency of Business
  Recommendations from Web-Search-Enabled Large Language Models (Exploratory Study)
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it using these metadata.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Pressfront Research
    city: Tampa
    region: Florida
    country: US
    website: https://pressfront.co/research
date-released: 2026-09-13
version: "1.0.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://github.com/jjoseph18/ai-recommendation-consistency
abstract: >-
  Ten open "best X for a small business" questions were each issued three times
  to ChatGPT (OpenAI Responses API with web_search) and Google Gemini
  (Generative Language API with Google Search grounding) on a single day, for 60
  responses total. From each response the set of recommended businesses was
  extracted and run-to-run consistency was measured as the mean pairwise Jaccard
  overlap of these sets across the three repetitions. Overall consistency was
  69.5% (ChatGPT 87.2%, Gemini 51.9%); of 127 distinct business-slots, 56%
  appeared in every repetition and 27% in only one. An exploratory study; the
  small sample means the results are directional. Full method, code, and all 60
  responses are released for independent verification. A formal preprint with a
  DOI is forthcoming on Zenodo.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - generative engine optimization
  - recommendation systems
  - reproducibility
  - ChatGPT
  - Gemini
